{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/ensure_pandoc.py","reason":"New: decode the bundled pandoc's Mach-O/ELF architecture, and on mismatch install the pinned, digest-verified upstream pandoc 3.9 into the git-ignored .tools/bin; also exposes repo_pandoc_for_host() for the test-time lookup."},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"New ensure-pandoc target modelled on the existing actionlint-bin pinned-binary install; make install invokes it after uv sync."},{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"Point PYPANDOC_PANDOC at .tools/bin/pandoc when it exists, is arch-matched, and the user has not set the variable; strict no-op otherwise."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_ensure_pandoc.py","reason":"New regression coverage: arch decoding for Mach-O and ELF, the no-op branch, the repair branch, the bad-digest refusal, and the pin-vs-accepted-digest drift guard."},{"path":"docs/local-dev-env.md","reason":"Replace the manual-only arm64 pandoc prerequisite with the automatic bootstrap path, keeping the manual steps as the offline fallback."},{"path":"NOTICE","reason":"Record that the dev bootstrap may fetch the same pandoc 3.9 from jgm/pandoc releases into a git-ignored directory; nothing becomes vendored or redistributed."}]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1793212808467083545,"uuid":"d292b43a-377e-47e4-a8de-f94a04088d82"}